282	     8	// **The checks** (G-47 (c)) are the core's first — `ReelGraphicPackage.read`,
283	     9	// the archive and its manifest — then the app's: a font must load in a
284	    10	// throwaway library, as `importFont` does, and an asset must be a name
285	    11	// `asset(name)` can use. Every refusal is "<file name> cannot be imported:
286	    12	// <sentence>", and none writes anything.
287	    13	//
288	    14	// **The plan** (G-47 (d)) puts each file under the manifest's name: written
289	    15	// when the name is free, reused when the file there holds the same bytes;
290	    16	// otherwise a module or a font takes `-2`, `-3`, … and an asset refuses the
291	    17	// import, because the module reaches it by name. A name is matched exactly:
292	    18	// one that differs only in case is another file, and is never free.
293	    19	//
294	    20	// **The copy** (G-47 (e)) writes the fonts, then the assets, with
295	    21	// `landNew` (never replacing), then the module with `write(name:bytes:)`; a
296	    22	// throw removes every file it wrote, rescans and rethrows. One `rescan()` at
297	    23	// the end, from the caller's handler or command — never from a
298	    24	// `.graphicsDidChange` observer. Not undoable and never dirty (G-3).
